│ patch_description        │ Replace the current-state greedy rule with a projected minimax rule: each candidate       │
│                          │ placement is scored by the maximum KVPR that would exist after placing the model, rather  │
│                          │ than by the GPU's KVPR before placement. This directly aligns every greedy decision with  │
│                          │ the objective.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Add a lightweight relocation improvement pass after the initial placement. It repeatedly  │
│                          │ moves a model from an overloaded GPU when doing so strictly reduces the global maximum    │
│                          │ KVPR while preserving memory feasibility. This corrects unfavorable early greedy choices  │
│                          │ without requiring an expensive exhaustive search over all placements.                     │
