│ patch_description        │ Add greedy initialization orders based on each model's standalone KVPR contribution,      │
│                          │ `weight / (GPU_MEM_SIZE - size)`. Unlike request-weight or weight-per-size ordering, this │
│                          │ directly captures the nonlinear pressure caused by consuming model memory. Models that    │
│                          │ leave little KV-cache capacity are therefore assigned early, when the placement has the   │
│                          │ most freedom. Additional complementary orders emphasize large high-pressure models and    │
│                          │ improve the chance that the existing local search starts from a better feasible basin     │
│                          │ without changing feasibility behavior.                                                    │
