│ patch_name               │ threshold_kvpr_packer                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The prior approach used four greedy orderings followed by up to 40 local relocation/swap  │
│                          │ iterations, but it directly optimized only the current greedy peak pressure. The new      │
│                          │ implementation treats a candidate maximum KVPR as a feasibility threshold. For threshold  │
│                          │ `T`, a GPU accepts a model only when both memory and `load <= T * remaining_memory`       │
│                          │ remain feasible. It uses six deterministic model orderings and three bin-selection modes, │
│                          │ then binary-searches the lowest feasible threshold for 38 iterations.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ A successful threshold packing immediately measures its actual maximum KVPR and tightens  │
│                          │ the binary-search upper bound to that measured value. This objective-aligned tightening   │
│                          │ avoids retaining slack from a feasible greedy assignment. A final 60-iteration            │
│                          │ relocation/swap improvement phase further improves the best threshold-generated           │
│                          │ placement.                                                                                │
