│ patch_description        │ Add a bounded two-model relocation repair when ordinary single moves and swaps cannot     │
│                          │ improve the current placement. A local optimum can require moving two models off the      │
│                          │ bottleneck GPU simultaneously: neither model may fit or improve alone, while their        │
│                          │ combined removal frees enough memory pressure to lower the global maximum KVPR. The       │
│                          │ repair only examines pairs from GPUs currently attaining the bottleneck and evaluates     │
│                          │ feasible target combinations, preserving the existing fast greedy and steepest-descent    │
│                          │ structure.                                                                                │
