│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ threshold_kvpr_packing                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ This version uses a pressure-threshold packing formulation rather than relying only on    │
│                          │ direct greedy KVPR placement. For a candidate maximum KVPR `T`, each GPU must satisfy     │
│                          │ `load / remaining_memory <= T`, which can be rewritten as `load + T * used_memory <= T *  │
│                          │ GPU_MEM_SIZE`. This turns the objective into a two-capacity packing problem: every GPU    │
│                          │ must satisfy both physical memory and transformed pressure capacity.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The algorithm first builds several reliable greedy placements, then performs a binary     │
│                          │ search over feasible pressure thresholds. At every threshold it evaluates multiple        │
│                          │ transformed-packing orderings and retains the assignment with the best true KVPR rather   │
│                          │ than returning the first feasible packing. Finally, it applies memory-feasible improving  │
│                          │ moves and swaps to polish the best assignment.                                            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
