│ patch_name               │ kvpr_binpack_refine                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The previous approach used multiple greedy orderings and 24 local-search passes, but it   │
│                          │ optimized KVPR only after placement. This version directly converts a target KVPR         │
│                          │ threshold `T` into an effective bin-packing size: `model_size + weight / T`. A placement  │
│                          │ is feasible at `T` when each GPU's effective size is at most 80 GB. Binary search over 32 │
│                          │ threshold iterations produces a substantially better balanced initial placement. It uses  │
│                          │ best-fit and first-fit decreasing variants, then runs 36 strictly improving move/swap     │
│                          │ refinement passes. Refinement accepts improvements to maximum KVPR, with the sorted       │
│                          │ GPU-pressure vector as a secondary tie-breaker.                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
