│ patch_description        │ The prior approach uses seven greedy orderings and up to 40 local-search iterations per   │
│                          │ ordering. Its key parameters are the ordering set, best-fit mode, and local-improvement   │
│                          │ iteration limit.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version directly searches for a low KVPR bound using transformed bin packing. For a  │
│                          │ proposed pressure bound `P`, each model has transformed weight `load + P * model_size`    │
│                          │ and every GPU has capacity `P * 80`. A packing within this capacity guarantees both       │
│                          │ memory feasibility and KVPR at most `P`. The algorithm performs 24 adaptive binary-search │
│                          │ rounds over this threshold, evaluates four transformed packing orders at every feasible   │
│                          │ threshold, retains the best actual KVPR placement, and then applies 60 lexicographic      │
│                          │ local-improvement steps. Lexicographic pressure comparison improves not only the worst    │
│                          │ GPU pressure but also secondary GPU pressures when the maximum is tied.                   │
