│ patch_description        │ This version keeps the effective-size threshold formulation, but improves feasibility     │
│                          │ detection near the binary-search boundary. Greedy bin packing can falsely reject a        │
│                          │ feasible threshold because of fragmentation. The new implementation tries several greedy  │
│                          │ orders and, when they fail, performs a bounded symmetry-pruned backtracking repair over   │
│                          │ the final models. For small instances it can search the complete effective-size packing   │
│                          │ directly.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It also retains multiple greedy KVPR seeds and applies move/swap local search to every    │
│                          │ feasible candidate, selecting the placement with the lowest maximum KVPR. All returned    │
│                          │ placements are concretely memory-feasible.                                                │
