│ patch_description        │ Add a third deterministic packing policy to threshold feasibility construction. Existing  │
│                          │ first-fit and best-fit policies only consider effective-size fragmentation. The new       │
│                          │ policy still enforces the effective-size capacity constraint required by the target KVPR, │
│                          │ but selects among feasible GPUs by the projected actual maximum KVPR. This produces       │
│                          │ different feasible seeds that are more aligned with the real objective, allowing the      │
│                          │ existing move/swap refinement to start from stronger placements while retaining the       │
│                          │ robust fragmentation-oriented policies as fallbacks.                                      │
